{y}_{0}=16\\,000>a=15\\,000,$ and ${y}_{0}=210>a=205.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395852 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3b512b5-d109-5b7f-afe6-8012cddf53df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=12\\,510-18P,\\,P(0)=690" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395854} {:answer/id #uuid "451e0e4f-f1c3-5f2c-a984-6761ce64e2da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.5P-1\\,23,\\,P(0)=2\\,500" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395855} {:answer/id #uuid "30e14fdd-8b43-5b70-9434-f7996dbad376" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=9P-6\\,066,\\,P(0)=680" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395856} {:answer/id #uuid "c372f938-bf0a-5da5-a0e8-947b58733787" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=2\\,580-0.6P,\\,P(0)=4\\,400" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395857} {:answer/id #uuid "848a4d3c-7246-5b73-b528-cdd85bf23fbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=16\\,256-4P,\\,P(0)=4\\,070" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3b512b5-d109-5b7f-afe6-8012cddf53df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=12\\,510-18P,\\,P(0)=690" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395854} :answer-field/id #uuid "f34c38b1-0c67-5df9-bd25-f72ef39097ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395853}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6960a095-e760-5362-9086-48e7e2e653fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-37180" :question/problem "Which of the following initial value problems is an inhibited growth problem?" :question/worked-solution "An inhibited growth initial value problem has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=k(a-y),\\,y(0)={y}_{0}\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ for all $t\\ge 0.$\n\nFrom the given options, the only inhibited growth problem is\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=12\\,510-18P,\\,P(0)=690,\n$$\n\nsince\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=12\\,510-18P=18(695-P).\n$$\n\nIn this case, $k=18,a=695,$ and ${y}_{0}=690.$ Notice that $a>{y}_{0},$ which is required for inhibited growth. \n\nThe other options do not represent inhibited growth. In particular, the initial value problems\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=16\\,256-4P=4(4\\,064-P),\\,P(0)=4\\,070,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=2\\,580-0.6P=0.6(4\\,300-P),\\,P(0)=4\\,400\n$$\n\ndo *not* represent an inhibited growth model because ${y}_{0}=4\\,070>a=4\\,064,$ and ${y}_{0}=4\\,400>a=4\\,300.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Inhibited Growth Equations and Initial Value Problems"}]}
